# Ratchets for rules (d) and (e) of scripts/lint-trap-tempfile-ownership.py (#7004).
# Companion to lint-trap-tempfile-ownership.highwater (shell class-b, rule (c)).
#
#   rule-d  non-test *.py / *.ts / *.mjs / *.js files that allocate scratch (mkdtemp*,
#           mkstemp, mktemp, NamedTemporaryFile(delete=False)) with NO cleanup construct and
#           NO owner marker. Runner-owned test files (test-shaped AND under a bunfig preload
#           / vitest globalSetup / conftest.py root) are counted separately as
#           `excluded-tests` in --census-detail and are not part of this number.
#   rule-e  files in any language whose scratch allocation carries a literal /tmp or
#           /var/tmp base (the 5 accepted today are production/CI shell scripts:
#           canary-bundle-claim-check.sh, ci-deploy.sh, credential-persist-home-guard.bench.sh,
#           push-infra-config.sh, file-upstream-ask-8160.sh).
#
# Derive with: python3 scripts/lint-trap-tempfile-ownership.py --census-detail
# CI (`--check-highwater`) asserts each live count never EXCEEDS its value here, AND that a
# change to a value in a diff moves the census by exactly that amount, measured against the
# MERGE-BASE copy of this file. Like the shell highwater, the census counts POPULATION and
# does not honour `lint-trap-ownership: ok`, so annotating a new site still shows up here and
# raising a value is a deliberate act that needs a reason in the PR body.
rule-d: 0
rule-e: 6
# 5 -> 6 (2026-10-20, #7376): the two new members are PLANTED guard-violation
# fixtures inside run-registered-suites.test.sh's T12 tmpns sweep (viol-tmp:
# `mktemp -d /tmp/fixed.XXXX`, viol-p-tmp: `mktemp -p /tmp`) — literal lines in
# <<'FIX' heredocs that exist only to prove the sweep fires. Each carries
# `lint-trap-ownership: ok planted guard-violation fixture`; the census counts
# population regardless of the escape. Bounded: the files live under $TMP and
# are reaped by the suite's EXIT trap.
